sentences.l:
and the whole of it was full of water poured out,
and many fine pieces of armour of young men slain in battle
floated, and corpses;

For I say that neither might will help, nor any form,
nor his fine armour, which, I suppose, very deep in the pool
will lie, covered under mud;

and you, along the banks of Xanthus,
burn the trees, and into him himself let go with fire; and let him not at all
turn you aside with gentle words, nor with threat;

Burned the elms and the willows and the tamarisks,
and burned the lotus and the rush and the sedge,
those which about the fair streams in plenty of the river had grown;

And as a cauldron boils within, pressed by a great fire,
melting the fat of a tender-fed pig,
from every side bubbling up, and beneath it dry sticks lie,
so his fair streams were burning with fire, and the water boiled;

sentences.t:
ἦ οὐ μέμνῃ ὅτε Τυδεΐδην Διομήδε’ ἀνῆκας
οὐτάμεναι, αὐτὴ δὲ πανόψιον ἔγχος ἑλοῦσα
ἰθὺς ἐμεῦ ὦσας, διὰ δὲ χρόα καλὸν ἔδαψας;

sentences.tr:
ē ou memnēi hote Tydeïdēn Diomēde’ anēkas
